  "landingFaqQ1": "How does farmer Mandi slot booking work?",
  "landingFaqA1": "Farmers select a 1-hour arrival window at their assigned Direct Procurement Centre (DPC). Automated scheduling reduces physical wait time to under 25 minutes.",
  "landingFaqQ2": "How are moisture and grain quality tested?",
  "landingFaqA2": "Centres use certified digital moisture analyzers and electronic weighbridges. The official Government MSP is credited directly without middleman deductions.",
  "landingFaqQ3": "When is the procurement amount credited to bank accounts?",
  "landingFaqA3": "Following electronic weighment certification, Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT via PFMS) releases funds to the farmer Aadhaar-linked account within 24 to 48 hours.",
  "landingFaqQ4": "Can farmers view live queue status prior to arrival?",
  "landingFaqA4": "Yes, farmers can check real-time queue tokens and estimated wait duration on this portal or via automated SMS alerts.",
  "landingFaqQ5": "What documents are required for produce registration?",
  "landingFaqA5": "Aadhaar card, Patta/Chitta land record documents, and an active Aadhaar-seeded bank account for DBT payment.",
